<title>UK: UK industrial output up 0.5 pct in July.</title>
<headline>UK industrial output up 0.5 pct in July.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics released the following seasonally adjusted data on UK industrial production in July:</p>
<p>    INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION	   JULY   JUNE    (PREL JUNE)</p>
<p>    Month-on-month change in pct   0.5   -0.9	(-1.1)</p>
<p>    Year-on-year change		0.9    0.9	(0.8)</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth change		 0.2    0.1	(0.2)</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth year ago change    1.0    1.0	(1.1)</p>
<p>    Index (Base 1990)		 106.9  106.4     (106.3)</p>
<p>MANUFACTURING OUTPUT</p>
<p>    Month-on-month change	    0.5   -0.1	(-0.3)</p>
<p>    Year-on-year change		0.3   -0.5	(-0.5)</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth change		unch   -0.2	(unch)</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth year ago change   -0.1   -0.1	(unch)</p>
<p>    Index (Base 1990)		 101.8  101.4     (101.3)</p>
<p>MINING/QUARRYING INCLUDING OIL AND GAS EXTRACTION</p>
<p>    Month-on-month change	    0.6   -2.4	(-2.3)</p>
<p>    Year-on-year change		2.3   10.7	(11.1)</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth change		 1.9    1.5	(1.4)</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth year ago change    5.9    5.2	(5.6)</p>
<p>    Index (Base 1990)		 143.3  142.4     (142.9)</p>
<p>ELECTRICITY, GAS AND WATER</p>
<p>    Month-on-month change	    0.3   -5.5	(-5.7)</p>
<p>    Year-on-year change		4.1    1.6	(1.3)</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth change		 0.5    1.0	(0.8)</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth year ago change    5.3    5.6	(5.5)</p>
<p>    Index (Base 1990)		 121.2  120.8     (120.5)</p>
<p>OIL AND GAS EXTRACTION</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth change		 2.9    n/a	(2.0)</p>
<p>    3-mth/3-mth year ago change    8.3    n/a	(7.6)</p>
<p>    Index (Base 1990)		 178.1  176.7     (177.6)</p>
<p>NOTE - Consensus forecast was for a 0.5 percent rise in industrial production in July, with a year-on-year rise of 0.8 percent. Manufacturing output was expected to rise 0.3 percent on the month.</p>
<p>The ONS said just over half of the manufacturing industries have shown increases in production in the three months to July. Most notable were rises of 1.7 percent in output of transport equipment industries, 0.8 percent in textiles, leather and clothing industries and 0.6 percent in the output of basic metals and metal products.</p>
</text>
